    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Bacteria are the most common cause of acute skeletal\ninfections, with Staphylococcus aureus being the most\ncommon organism across all age groups, including\nnewborns.\nIn neonates, group B streptococcus and Gram-negative\nenteric bacilli such as Escherichia coli are also important\npathogens, while group A streptococcus accounts for less than\n10% of cases.\nAfter age 6, most osteomyelitis cases are due to S. aureus,\ngroup A streptococci, or Pseudomonas aeruginosa.",
