    "explanation": "Optic neuritis is associated with ethambutol.\nAdverse reactions\nRifampicin\n• Orange discoloration of secretions or urine\n• Staining of contact lenses\n• Influenza-like reaction\n• Thrombocytopenia\n• Pruritus\nEthambutol\n• Optic neuritis (reversible)\n• Decreased red-green color discrimination\n• GI tract disturbances\n• Hypersensitivity\nIsoniazid\n• Mild hepatic enzyme elevation\n• Hepatitis\n• Peripheral neuritis\n• Hypersensitivity\nPyrazinamide\n• Hepatotoxic effects\n• Hyperuricemia\n• Arthralgias",
