    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 85,
    "stem": "During which period of gestation is\nTdap vaccination optimally\nrecommended to maximize passive\nantibody transfer to the newborn?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "20–26 weeks"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "27–36 weeks"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "37–40 weeks"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Immediately postpartum"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "Pregnant women should receive Tdap during each pregnancy\nto confer passive antibody protection to the infant until they\ncan receive DTaP.\nOptimal administration of Tdap is recommended early in the\nperiod between 27 and 36 weeks of gestation to ensure\nmaximal antibody concentration at birth.",
