      "C": "This statement is accurate. Nighttime cough can be indicative of conditions affecting the upper airway, such as sinusitis or postnasal drip. It highlights the role of upper airway issues in chronic cough.",
      "D": "This statement is FALSE. The receptors for chronic cough are primarily located in the upper respiratory tract. Conditions affecting the upper airway, like postnasal drip, sinusitis, or irritants in the throat, can trigger chronic cough reflexes."
