    "explanation": "The boot-shaped heart sign is a conventional radiographic finding in patients with TOF. The toe of the boot is formed by the upward pointing cardiac apex, which makes an acute angle with the diaphragm. The upturned cardiac apex is ascribed to right ventricular hypertrophy and occurs in 65% of patients with TOF.",
