    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Photopsia is a classic symptom associated with migraine aura. It refers to the perception of flashes of light or flickering lights. This visual disturbance is one of the characteristic features of migraine aura.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Tinnitus, or ringing in the ears, is not typically associated with migraine aura. Migraine aura commonly involves visual disturbances, sensory changes, and sometimes motor symptoms.",
      "B": "Abdominal symptoms can be part of a migraine attack, especially in pediatric cases, where it's referred to as abdominal migraine. However, for the typical aura, abdominal symptoms are not a common feature.",
      "C": "Photopsia is a classic symptom associated with migraine aura. It refers to the perception of flashes of light or flickering lights. This visual disturbance is one of the characteristic features of migraine aura.",
      "D": "While motion sickness and migraine can share triggers, such as sensitivity to sensory stimuli, motion sickness is not typically considered an aura symptom of migraine."
    },
