    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 19,
    "stem": "A 12 year old male presents with complaints of\npolyarthritis and an evanescent rash which spares\nthe face. On PE, patient appears to be in respiratory\ndistress and auscultation revealed tachycardia and\na gallop rhythm, and some hard painless freely\nmovable swellings over the extensor surfaces like\nthe elbows. Chest xray reveals cardiomegaly and\nASOT is 350 Todd units. The following are\nappropriate in the management of this patient\nexcept:",
