    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 90,
    "stem": "10. A 25 year old G3P2 (2002) mother, KEC, was\nadmitted to VCMC hospital due to hyperemesis\ngravidarum. Her 2 year old child started to have\nintensely pruritic erythematous macules that\nevolve through papules then vesicles distributed\ncentripetally 2 days ago. KEC also has a 12 month\nold child at home and a 14 year old neighbor who\ngot exposed. Which of the following is the most\nappropriate management?",
