    "id": "superexam-pediatrics-0094",
    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 94,
    "stem": "14. RL, a 16 year old male, came in for recurrent\ntonsilitis 5x this year. Patient underwent bilateral\ntonsillectomy and during the 1st postoperative day,\nrecurrent bleeding at operative site was noted.\nLaboratories requested were as follows: bleeding\ntime = 3 minutes (2 - 8); PTT= 78 seconds (21 - 35);\nINR = 1.0; mixing studies = correction of PTT; CBC\nand thrombin time within normal limits. Which of\nthe following is the most likely diagnosis?",
