    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 95,
    "stem": "15. A 7 year old male came in for high grade fever 6\ndays PTC associated with a polymorphous rash,\ndiffuse injection of pharynx, cervical\nlymphadenopathy, and periungual peeling of toes.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate\nmanagement for this patient?",
