    "stem": "A 6 y/o boy developed anasarca. On PE, BP 100/70\n(p50). Laboratory findings showed Urine protein\non dipstick 4+, Urine protein/urine creatinine ratio\nwas elevated. He was started on oral prednisone.\nAfter 2 weeks upon follow up, the edema resolved\nand urinalysis was normal. If this is a nephrotic\nsyndrome, it fits the course of:",
