    "explanation": "APGAR score=5; 8-10 good cardiopulmonary\nadaptation, 4-7 need for rescucitation esp. ventilatory\nsupport; 0-3 immediate rescucitation. The APGAR\nscore helps to rapidly assess th need to rescucitate\nneonates after birth. SIMILAR TO PREVIOUS BOARD\nEXAM CONCEPT.",
