    "originalNumber": 203,
    "stem": "Which among the following patients with measles is\nmost likely to develop SSPE?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "A 2 year-old male patient"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "A 6 year-old patient who was not given vitamin\nA"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "A 10 year-old patient who has developed\npneumonia"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "A 14 year-old patient who is\nimmunocompromised"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "A 16 year-old with subclinical measles"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "Measles at an early age favors the development of\nSSPE. 50% of SSPE patients had primary measles\nbefore 2 years of age and 75% before 4 years of age.\nMales are affected twice as often as females.",
