    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 235,
    "stem": "A 6 y/o female presents with a 2 day history of\npainless blood stained stool. During the consult,\npatient is comfortable and denies any feeling of\npain. abdominal examination is normal. However,\nshe has pale palpebral conjunctiva and noted to be\ntachycardic for her age. what is the best initial test\nto request to establish your diagnosis?",
