    "id": "superexam-pediatrics-0292",
    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 292,
    "stem": "Which of the following statements best describes a\n\"physiologic\" jaundice in the newborn?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Direct bilirubin >10% of the total bilirubin"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Present in the first 24 hours of life"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Resolves on the 10th day of life"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Rate of rise of bilirubin is 6 mg/dL/24hr"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "None of the above"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Pathologic jaundice: (1) it appears in the 1st 24–36 hr\nof life, (2) serum bilirubin is rising at a rate faster than\n5 mg/dL/24 hr, (3) serum bilirubin is >12 mg/dL in\nfull-term infants (especially in the absence of risk\nfactors) or 10–14 mg/dL in preterm infants, (4)\njaundice persists after 10–14 days of life, or (5) direct-\nreacting bilirubin is >2 mg/dL at any time.",
