    "stem": "A 4-year old male was brought to the ER after\npassing tea-colored urine. Patient was also noted to\nhave periorbaital edema and with BP of 130/90.\nUrinalysis revealed 2-3 RBC casts. Mother insists\nthat the child has no history of recent pharyngeal or\noral infections. To support your hint that this is a\ncase of cutaneous PSGN you would order for:",
