    "id": "superexam-pediatrics-0434",
    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 434,
    "stem": "A 2-year old female patient was diagnosed with\niron deficiency anemia. Iron supplement therapy\nwas immediately instituted. At what time after\nbeginning of treatment do you expect hemoglobin\nto increase?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "1 day"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "3 days"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "6 weeks"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "3 months"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Ferrous sulfate is given at a dose 6 mg/kg/day\n(elemental iron). Subjective improvement is expected\nafter 12-24 hours; preliminary BM response after 48\nhours; increase in reticulocyte count after 72 hours;\nhemoglobin increase after 4-6 weeks; and repletion of\niron stores after 3 months.",
