    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "Bitot's spots are the buildup of keratin debris located\nsuperficially in the conjunctiva, which are oval,\ntriangular or irregular in shape. These spots are a sign\nof vitamin A deficiency and are associated with\nconjunctival xerosis. Kayser–Fleischer rings are dark\nrings that appear to encircle the iris of the eye due to\ncopper deposition in part of the cornea as a result of\nparticular liver diseases.",
