    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 490,
    "stem": "5-month-old Maricel presented at the emergency\nroom with irritability, repeated bouts of crying, and\nintermittent colicky abdominal pain. On physical\nexamination, there is a sausage-shaped mass in the\nright upper quadrant. There is empty rectal vault\non DRE, with blood per examining finger. What is\nthe most likely diagnosis?",
