    "stem": "A 16-year-old girl is brought to the physician\nbecause of episodes of palpitations over the past 6\nmonths. The episodes occur when she runs or plays\nbasketball. She is otherwise asymptomatic. Her\nblood pressure is 124/46 mm Hg, pulse is 78/min,\nand respirations are 18/min. She weighs 55 kg\n(121 lb) and is 180 cm (71 in) tall. Her arm span is\n188 cm (74 in), and the upper segment to lower\nsegment ratio is 0.85. Her fingers appear long and\nare hyperextensible. A grade 4/6, early diastolic\nmurmur is heard along the upper and middle left\nsternal border with radiation to the apex.\nPeripheral pulses are bounding. Which of the\nfollowing is the most likely cause of these findings?",
