    "id": "superexam-pediatrics-0556",
    "subject": "pediatrics",
    "originalNumber": 556,
    "stem": "A term infant, delivered via cesarean section, is\nreferred to you for tachypnea and expiratory\ngrunting at the first hour of life. Otherwise, physical\nexamination is unremarkable. You order a stat CXR\nwhich revealed prominent vascular markings and\nfluid in intralobar fissures. Which of the following is\nthe MOST IMPORTANT predisposing factor in this\ncondition?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Birth by cesarean delivery"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Low birthweight"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Prolonged labor"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Administration of large amounts of IV fluids to\nthe mother"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "Birth to a diabetic mother"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "Patient has transient tachypnea of the newborn.\nPremature birth, precipitous birth, and operative birth\nwithout labor have all been associated with an\nincreased risk of TTN.",
