    "stem": "An 11- month old infant was brought to you clinic\ndue to fever irritability. On physical examination,\nPR 100, RR 25, temp 37.9. The nasal turbintaes\nwere erythematous and congested without\npurulent discharge. On otoscopy, the tympanic\nmembrane was bulging, amber-clored, and with air\nbubbles behind the tympanic membrane. If you are\nconsidering acute otitis media, what is the dose of\namoxicillin that you will give to your patient?",
