    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "Injury to the brachial plexus may cause paralysis of\nthe upper part of the arm with or without paralysis of\nthe forearm or hand or, more commonly, paralysis of\nthe entire arm. In Erb-Duchenne paralysis, the injury\nis limited to the 5th and 6th cervical nerves. The\ncharacteristic position consists of adduction and\ninternal rotation of the arm with pronation of the\nforearm. Power to extend the forearm is retained, but\nthe biceps reflex is absent; the Moro reflex is absent\non the affected side.",
