    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "APGAR scoring is as follows (0, 1, 2)\nHeart rate: Absent, Below 100, Over 100\nRespiratory effort: Absent; Slow, irregular; Good,\ncrying\nMuscle tone: Limp; Some flexion of extremities; Active\nmotion\nResponse to catheter in nostril (tested after\noropharynx is clear): No response; Grimace; Cough or\nsneeze\nColor: Blue, pale; Body pink, extremities blue;\nCompletely pink",
