    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "Answer: A. Penicillin\nNotes: Neonatal tetanus is an acute spastic paralystic\nillness caused by the neurotoxin (Tetanospasmin)\nproduced by Clostridium tetani. In infants causes\nprogressive difficulty in feeding, associated hunger\nand crying. In older children, causes trismus, sardonic\nsmile. Treatment includes Human Tetanus Ig, PCN G\n(DOC), surgery.",
