    "originalNumber": 696,
    "stem": "A 19-yr old primi develops toxemia in her last\ntrimester of pregnancy and during the course of her\nlabor ,is treated with MgSO4. At 38 weeks AOG, she\ndelivers a 2100gms infant with APGAR score of 1 at\n1 min. And 5 at 5 mins. At 18 hrs of age, hematocrit\nwas 79%, plt.ct. 100,000/uL, glucose 38 mg/dl, Mg\n2.5 mEq/L, Ca 8.7 mg/dl. Soon after, infant has a\ngeneralized convulsion. The most likely cause is",
